        "**Parkinsonism (MDS 2015):** **bradykinesia** - slowness of movement WITH decrement in amplitude or speed on repetitive movement - plus **at least one** of **rest tremor** or **rigidity**. Bradykinesia is mandatory: no decrement, no parkinsonism.",
        "The classical teaching tetrad is **TRAP** - Tremor at rest, Rigidity, Akinesia/bradykinesia, Postural instability - but postural instability is a **late** feature of Parkinson's disease and is deliberately excluded from the modern definition because early falls point away from idiopathic disease.",
