        "**Epidemiology:** age is the dominant risk factor - about **1% of people over 60** and 3-4% over 80; mean onset around 60 years; men are affected about 1.5 times as often as women. Indian door-to-door surveys vary widely (roughly 30-70 per 100,000 in most, but 328 per 100,000 in the Parsi community of Mumbai), so quote the range, not one number.",
