    "Before diagnosing Parkinson's disease in an Indian outpatient, **ask what tablets have been taken for gas, acidity, giddiness or headache** - levosulpiride, metoclopramide, flunarizine and cinnarizine make drug-induced parkinsonism the commonest reversible cause seen in general practice.",
    "**Postural instability is late.** Falls in the first year mean progressive supranuclear palsy; autonomic failure in the first years means multiple system atrophy; dementia in the first year means Lewy body dementia.",
